        {
          "title": "Two Hundred",
          "subtitle": "Card Game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "200 (Deux Cents) is a point-trick partnership card game from Canada, especially popular in New Brunswick. Four players use a 36-card deck (2s, 3s, 4s, 6s removed). Teams bid in increments of 5 (50-100); highest bidder names trump and must make their bid. First team to 200 points wins."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Likely originated in Canada; played in New Brunswick for at least 3-4 generations (1930s or earlier). Closely related to Rook (Parker Brothers 1906); possibly Rook was based on 200 or both share a common ancestor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4 (partnerships, partners opposite)"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36 cards (A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 5 per suitâ€”remove 2s, 3s, 4s, 6s)"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card deck, score sheet"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "All cards dealt (9 each); bidding then play."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
